def lens_prompt(slug: str, out_dir: Path, lens: str) -> str:
    if lens == "likeness":
        ref = out_dir / "reference" / "concept.png"
        concept = ref if ref.is_file() else out_dir / "concept.png"
        method = f"""The harness re-rendered the CURRENT geometry into `{slug}_review/` just
before this session — the renders on disk are fresh. Do NOT re-render, do NOT
run the review script. READ (view) `{slug}_review/_parts_colored.png` (if it
exists — the assembly with each part in its brief color, so a missing part is a
missing COLOR: name it) plus `{slug}_review/_assembled.png` and
`{slug}_review/_qa.png` next to `{concept}` and compare them directly. Do NOT
edit part files — verdict only.

This lens is VISUAL-ONLY: judge silhouette, overall proportions, feature
presence/placement and part character — would a stranger say these show the
SAME OBJECT? The concept is a generated photograph and the renders are
flat-shaded CAD, so material, colour, lighting, background and camera framing
